{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"yes\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"Signal analysis during 15 trials containing freezing or significant motor output slowing precipitated by dual‐tasking demonstrated reduced θ frequency (3–8 Hz) firing compared to 18 unaffected trials.\",\n    \"Specifically, we observed reduced θ activity coincident with cue presentation for trials where ongoing VR gait was disturbed by concurrent cognitive processing (either VR freezing or >50% FPV reduction), compared to trials that were unaffected by dual‐tasking (Fig. 2).\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"The remaining 15 trials were pooled and classed as cognitive cue‐associated VR freezing (n = 8) or significant VR gait slowing where there was >50% FPV reduction (n = 7).\",\n    \"Further research is required to explore whether the presently reported reduction in θ frequency activity relates specifically to altered cognitive processing or to freezing itself.\",\n    \"A remaining challenge for future work is to confirm our preliminary findings in a larger cohort and discern robust features that distinguish pathological freezing and gait disturbances with cognitive dual‐tasking.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的解释有部分依据，但存在重要限定条件。论文确实将STN theta活动下降置于认知负荷诱发的FOG及步态障碍的研究背景下，因此将其作为FOG相关神经活动的证据并非完全错误。然而，关键分析中的15个受影响试次并非全部为实际冻结试次，而是合并了8个冻结试次和7个显著步态减速试次（FPV下降超过50%）。因此，theta活动下降反映的是认知负荷相关步态功能障碍这一混合结果，不能直接等同于FOG特异性神经活动变化。指控者的描述有明确全文依据。尤其是作者明确指出，仍需进一步研究该theta活动下降究竟与认知加工改变有关，还是与冻结本身有关。这表明作者并未将观察到的神经活动变化确认为FOG特异性现象。需要准确区分的是，冻结和显著步态减速是汇总分析中两类不同的受影响试次，并非每个受影响试次都同时出现冻结和显著减速。总体判断：报告将该发现用于FOG机制比较具有一定依据，但若未交代7个显著步态减速试次的纳入，确实遗漏了影响FOG特异性解释的重要限定；指控者关于不能将结果简单解释为实际FOG特异性神经活动变化的判断成立。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "28d0110f-8e1c-49a5-a857-cec4484d43b3", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261114T204324953299Z", "elapsed_seconds": 77.328, "completed_utc": "2026-11-14T20:44:42.296543+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "06ee876c64f05ed62e953f9134e1736204a72d64e7c2d024269edfde1764f9b9", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "yi/local-codex-auth", "account_sha256": "b3efb6361563c139233ed7b7ef61a7c9afe0bd48d4eb3525dbe31956b024d6da", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261114T204324953299Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "a275d0c30d17f4974678befb160ca1f8ac6168c5655c6e289665bd4a2025b29e"}}}
